### ✅ **Correct Loki Log Query for Exception Detection (UI Pod)**

If `|= "Exception"` didn’t work, try using a **case-insensitive regex match** with `|~`:

```logql
count_over_time({
  cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001",
  namespace="storefront-storefront-ut",
  pod=~"mobility-ops-storefront-poc-ut-.*"
} |~ "(?i)exception" [1h])
```

> ✅ This will match **Exception**, **exception**, or even `EXCEPTION` regardless of case.

